ild output\n├── cmake/                             # CMake toolchain\n└── Config/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. ALL MOTOR-RELATED FILES (Complete List)\n\n| # | File (absolute path) | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1** | `.../Development_Layer/External_Device/Motor/Motor_DM.h` | **DM motor class header** — Defines `Class_Motor_DM_Normal` (traditional mode) and `Class_Motor_DM_1_To_4` (\"one-to-four\" mode). Contains all motor enums (`Enum_Motor_DM_Status`, `Enum_Motor_DM_Motor_ID_1_To_4`, `Enum_Motor_DM_Control_Status_Normal`, `Enum_Motor_DM_Control_Method`), data structures for CAN RX/TX, and all inline getters/setters for angle, omega, torque, current, K_P, K_D. |\n| **2** | `.../Development_Layer/External_Device/Motor/Motor_DM.cpp` | **DM motor class implementation** — Full motor logic: `Init()` (binds CAN, configures IDs/method), `CAN_RxCpltCallback()` (receive), `CAN_Send_Enter/Exit/Clear_Error/Save_Zero()` (enable/disable/clear/save-zero), `Data_Process()` (decodes CAN data), `Output()` (encodes CAN frames for MIT/Angle-Omega/Omega/EMIT modes), `RTOS_100ms_Alive_Callback()` (alive check), `RTOS_Send_Callback()` (periodic control send), `Dog_Send_Callback()` (dog-specific control), `RTOS_Calculate_Callback()` (PID calc + output for 1-to-4 mode). |\n| **3** | `.../Development_Layer/Robot_Control/Foot_Control/foot_control.h` | **Single-leg control class header** — Defines `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM` which contains **two DM motors** per leg: `mi` (inner motor) and `mo` (outer motor). Functions: `SingleFoot_Init()`, `FootXY_map_MotorAngle()` (inverse kinematics), `Foot_control()`, `Set_x_y()`. |\n| **4** | `.../Development_Layer/Robot_Control/Foot_Control/foot_control.cpp` | **Single-leg control implementation** — `SingleFoot_Init()` calls `mo.Init()` and `mi.Init()`, sets K_P/K_D. `FootXY_map_MotorAngle()` performs 2-DOF leg inverse kinematics. `Foot_control()` calls IK mapping then `mi.Dog_Send_Callback()` + `mo.Dog_Send_Callback()`. |\n| **5** | `.../Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_RobotDog/robotdog_class.h` | **Robot dog class header** — Declares `CLASS_DOG` with **four leg objects**: `Foot1_Left_Back`, `Foot2_Right_Back`, `Foot3_Left_Front`, `Foot4_Right_Front`. |\n| **6** | `.../Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_RobotDog/robotdog_class.cpp` | **Robot dog class implementation** — `Chassis_Init()` assigns CAN IDs to each foot. `Chassis_Control()` calls `Foot_control()` twice per foot per cycle. |\n| **7** | `.../Development_Layer/Driver/CAN/drv_can.h` | **CAN driver header** — Defines `Struct_CAN_Manage_Object`, `Struct_CAN_Rx_Buffer`, `CAN_Call_Back` function pointer type, `CAN_Send_Data()`, `CAN_Send_Data_Realtime()`, `CAN_Init()`, `CAN_Update_Bus_Status()`, `RTOS_1ms_CAN_Motor_Callback()`. Declares `CAN1_Manage_Object` and `CAN2_Manage_Object`. Also declares all CAN TX buffers (e.g., `CAN1_0x200_Tx_Data`, `CAN2_0x1ff_Tx_Data`, etc.). |\n| **8** | `.../Development_Layer/Driver/CAN/drv_can.cpp` | **CAN driver implementation** — Full CAN initialization with 2 filter banks, interrupt-driven RX (FIFO0 for filtered IDs 0x200-0x20F, FIFO1 for all other IDs), TX with retry logic, bus-off recovery. `HAL_CAN_RxFifo0Callback()` and `HAL_CAN_RxFifo1Callback()` dispatch to upper-layer callback functions. |\n| **9** | `.../Development_Layer/Task/CallBack_Task/callback_task.h` | **Callback task header** — Declares `Robot_Init()`, `Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()`, `CAN1_Callback()`. |\n| **10** | `.../Development_Layer/Task/CallBack_Task/callback_task.cpp` | **Callback task implementation** — `Robot_Init()` calls `CAN_Init(&hcan1, CAN1_Callback)` then `dog.Chassis_Init()`. `Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()` (1ms timer) sets `Set_x_y(0.01, 0.06)` on Foot1_Left_Back and calls `dog.Chassis_Control()`. `CAN1_Callback()` dispatches received CAN frames to the correct motor's `CAN_RxCpltCallback()` based on StdId matching each foot's inner/outer motor RX ID. |\n| **11** | `.../Core/Inc/can.h` | **HAL CAN header** — Declares `hcan1`, `hcan2` and `MX_CAN1_Init()`, `MX_CAN2_Init()`. |\n| **12** | `.../Core/Src/can.c` | **HAL CAN configuration** — Hardware init for CAN1 (PD0=RX, PD1=TX) and CAN2 (PB5=RX, PB6=TX). Prescaler=6, BS1=3, BS2=3 → ~1Mbps. MSP init/deinit with NVIC priority 1 for all CAN interrupts. |\n| **13** | `.../Core/Src/main.c` | **Main entry point** — Calls `MX_CAN1_Init()`, `MX_CAN2_Init()`, `MX_TIM6_Init()`, then `Robot_Init()` after a 2-second delay. Infinite loop in `while(1)`. |\n| **14** | `.../Development_Layer/Robot_Control/Controller/PID.h` | **PID controller header** — Used by `Class_Motor_DM_1_To_4` for angle and velocity PID control loops. |\n| **15** | `.../Development_Layer/Driver/Math/drv_math.h` | **Math utilities** — Provides `Math_Constrain()`, `Math_Endian_Reverse_16/32()`, `Math_Float_To_Int()`, `Math_Int_To_Float()`, constants like `RPM_TO_RADPS`, `CELSIUS_TO_KELVIN`. Used extensively in motor data processing. |\n| **16** | `.../Development_Layer/Driver/Tim/drv_tim.cpp` | **Timer driver** — `HAL_TIM_PeriodElapsedCallback()` dispatches to registered callback functions. TIM6 is used for the 1ms robot control loop. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. REFERENCES TO \"Foot1_Left_Back\" AND MOTOR IDENTIFIERS\n\n**`Foot1_Left_Back` is the primary instance name** for the left-back leg's `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM` object.\n\n| Location | Reference |\n|---|---|\n| `robotdog_class.h:19` | `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM Foot1_Left_Back;` (declaration) |\n| `robotdog_class.cpp:30` | `Foot1_Left_Back.SingleFoot_Init(&hcan1,0x11,0x01,&hcan1,0x12,0x02,2,0.01,0.0,0.01,0.01);` |\n| `robotdog_class.cpp:52-53` | `Foot1_Left_Back.Foot_control();` (called twice) |\n| `callback_task.cpp:52` | `dog.Foot1_Left_Back.Set_x_y(0.01,0.06);` |\n| `callback_task.cpp:68` | `dog.Foot1_Left_Back.mi.Get_CAN_Rx_ID()` (in CAN1 callback) |\n| `callback_task.cpp:84` | `dog.Foot1_Left_Back.mo.Get_CAN_Rx_ID()` (in CAN1 callback) |\n\n**All four leg motor identifiers and their CAN assignments:**\n\n| Leg Object | CAN Bus | Inner Motor (mi) | Outer Motor (mo) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Foot1_Left_Back` | hcan1 | RX=0x11, TX=0x01 | RX=0x12, TX=0x02 |\n| `Foot2_Right_Back` | hcan1 | RX=0x14, TX=0x04 | RX=0x13, TX=0x03 |\n| `Foot3_Left_Front` | hcan1 | RX=0x18, TX=0x08 | RX=0x17, TX=0x07 |\n| `Foot4_Right_Front` | hcan1 | RX=0x15, TX=0x05 | RX=0x16, TX=0x06 |\n\n---\n\n### 4. INITIALIZATION, ENABLE/DISABLE, AND COMMAND-SENDING CODE PATHS\n\n#### Initialization chain:\n```\nmain.c:108 → Robot_Init()\n  → callback_task.cpp:18 → CAN_Init(&hcan1, CAN1_Callback)   [CAN bus init + callback registration]\n  → callback_task.cpp:20 → dog.Chassis_Init()\n      → robotdog_class.cpp:30-33 → FootX.SingleFoot_Init(...) for all 4 feet\n          → foot_control.cpp:20-21 → mo.Init(...) + mi.Init(...)\n              → Motor_DM.cpp:40 → Class_Motor_DM_Normal::Init() [binds CAN object, sets IDs, limits, method]\n          → foot_control.cpp:25-35 → mo.Set_K_P/K_D + mi.Set_K_P/K_D + control angle/omega/torque defaults\n```\n\n#### Enable/Disable code:\n- **Enable**: `Motor_DM.cpp:237-239` — `CAN_Send_Enter()` sends `{0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xfc}` over CAN\n- **Disable**: `Motor_DM.cpp:246-248` — `CAN_Send_Exit()` sends `{0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xfd}` over CAN\n- **Clear Error**: `Motor_DM.cpp:228-230` — `CAN_Send_Clear_Error()` sends `{0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xfb}`\n- **Save Zero**: `Motor_DM.cpp:255-257` — `CAN_Send_Save_Zero()` sends `{0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xfe}`\n- **Auto-enable on disconnect**: `Motor_DM.cpp:299-302` — In `RTOS_Send_Callback()` and `Dog_Send_Callback()`, if motor status is `DISABLE`, calls `CAN_Send_Enter()` to re-enable\n\n#### Command-sending paths:\n1. **`Dog_Send_Callback()`** (Motor_DM.cpp:315-339) — Called from `foot_control.cpp:113-114` during each Foot_control() cycle. Constrains all control values, then calls `Output()`.\n2. **`RTOS_Send_Callback()`** (Motor_DM.cpp:285-309) — Alternative periodic send path.\n3. **`Output()`** (Motor_DM.cpp:401-464) — Encodes control data per the selected control method (MIT / Angle-Omega / Omega / EMIT) and calls `CAN_Send_Data()`.\n\n#### Lifecycle monitoring:\n- **`RTOS_100ms_Alive_Callback()`** (Motor_DM.cpp:264-278) — Called every 100ms. If no CAN frame was received since last check, sets `Motor_DM_Status = DISABLE`. Otherwise `ENABLE`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. CAN BUS COMMUNICATION CODE FOR MOTORS\n\n#### Low-level CAN Driver (`drv_can.cpp`):\n\n| Function | Line | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CAN_Init()` | 106-158 | Configures two filter banks: Filter 0 (mask 0x7F0 → FIFO0 for IDs 0x200-0x20F), Filter 1 (accept-all → FIFO1). Activates RX FIFO0/1, error, and TX mailbox empty interrupts. Calls HAL_CAN_Start. |\n| `CAN_Send_Data()` | 168-200 | Sends a standard CAN frame with retry (up to 200 attempts ~2ms). Updates TX statistics. |\n| `CAN_Send_Data_Realtime()` | 210-222 | Checks if TX mailbox is available first, no retry. |\n| `HAL_CAN_RxFifo0Callback()` | 297-321 | ISR: reads from FIFO0, calls `manager_obj->Callback_Function()` |\n| `HAL_CAN_RxFifo1Callback()` | 328-352 | ISR: reads from FIFO1, calls `manager_obj->Callback_Function()` |\n| `HAL_CAN_ErrorStatusCallback()` | 360-392 | Handles warning/passive/bus-off with auto-recovery |\n| `CAN_Update_Bus_Status()` | 228-263 | Reads MSR/ESR registers for protocol status |\n| `RTOS_1ms_CAN_Motor_Callback()` | 281-290 | **Currently empty** (commented-out DJI motor send code) |\n\n#### CAN1 Callback → Motor Dispatch (`callback_task.cpp:64-105`):\n\nThe `CAN1_Callback()` function is the **central dispatcher** for all motor CAN RX. It checks `CAN_RxMessage->Header.StdId` against each motor's `Get_CAN_Rx_ID()` and routes to the appropriate motor's `CAN_RxCpltCallback()`:\n\n```\nif (ID == Foot1_Left_Back.mi) → Foot1_Left_Back.mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot2_Right_Back.mi) → Foot2_Right_Back.mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot3_Left_Front.mi) → Foot3_Left_Front.mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot4_Right_Front.mi) → Foot4_Right_Front.mi.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot1_Left_Back.mo) → Foot1_Left_Back.mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot2_Right_Back.mo) → Foot2_Right_Back.mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot3_Left_Front.mo) → Foot3_Left_Front.mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\nif (ID == Foot4_Right_Front.mo) → Foot4_Right_Front.mo.CAN_RxCpltCallback()\n```\n\n**Important note:** Currently only CAN1 callback is implemented. There is no CAN2 callback registered. Also, there is no CAN2 callback function declared (only `CAN1_Callback` exists).\n\n#### CAN Hardware Configuration (`can.c`):\n\n- **CAN1**: PD0 (RX), PD1 (TX) — Prescaler=6, BS1=3TQ, BS2=3TQ → effective baud rate = 42MHz / (6*(1+3+3)) = **1Mbps**\n- **CAN2**: PB5 (RX), PB6 (TX) — Same timing config, but **AutoRetransmission = DISABLE** (vs CAN1's ENABLE)\n- Both have AutoBusOff = DISABLE, all interrupt priorities = 1\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Key Architectural Points\n\n1. **Motor type**: **DM (达妙) motors** — Chinese brushless DC motors with CAN interface. Two protocol modes: \"Normal\" (traditional DM protocol) and \"1-to-4\" (DJI-style daisy-chain).\n\n2. **Each leg has 2 motors** (inner `mi` and outer `mo`), controlled via `Class_SingleDogFoot_DM`.\n\n3. **Control loop**: The 1ms TIM6 interrupt fires `Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()` → sets foot XY position → calls `Chassis_Control()` → each foot runs `Foot_control()` → inverse kinematics → `Dog_Send_Callback()` → `Output()` → `CAN_Send_Data()`.\n\n4. **All 8 motors** (4 legs × 2 motors) are on **CAN1** bus. The CAN IDs range from 0x01 to 0x18.\n\n5. **Enable is automatic**: If a motor stops responding, `Dog_Send_Callback()` detects DISABLE status and sends `CAN_Send_Enter()` to re-enable it."
